**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The remedy for a library of another schema: recreate it, the old file kept in `Backups` first (001 §C 'No migrations': the remedy is to recreate the database from the catalogues; the S2.4 brief: the old file is first copied into `Backups/`, then deleted and recreated; .spec-md §7 '`Test` EF table + migration → library model'). In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs` (step 86): `type LibraryDatabase with static member recreate (connectionString : ConnectionString) (backups : FolderName) (now : unit -> LibraryBackupTime) : Result<LibraryDatabase, StorageError>`, marked `StorageBoundary` as step 86's member is, its doc one to three lines. It reads the connection string through `SqliteConnectionStringBuilder`. An in-memory library (`DataSource` `:memory:` or `Mode` `Memory`) has no file, so it answers `LibraryDatabase.openOrCreate connectionString`. For a file library whose file exists, it creates `backups` when missing, copies the file to the next backup name of step 86's rule (`File.Copy`, never overwriting), then deletes the file and any `-wal`, `-shm` and `-journal` file beside it, and answers `openOrCreate connectionString`, which creates and stamps a new library (`CreatedLibraryDatabase`, step 84). A missing file is simply created. Every IO failure is caught and answered as `FileIoExn`; a failed copy deletes nothing. It runs on a file no handle holds: its caller has none, because `openOrCreate` disposed the connection when it answered the mismatch (step 62). No retry, rename-instead-of-copy or migration is added. Tests, in `LibraryDatabaseTests`, under step 84's folder: `recreate copies the old library file into the backups folder, then creates a new stamped library`: a file library whose stamp a plain connection set to 2 (step 62's way) answers `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr` from `openOrCreate`; `recreate` under a fixed clock answers `Ok` a `CreatedLibraryDatabase` stamped 1 and holding no entry; `Backups` beside it holds exactly `library-<stamp>.db`, whose stamp a plain connection reads as 2; and no `-wal` or `-shm` file of the old library is left. `recreate of an in-memory library creates a new one and copies nothing`: `recreate` of `Data Source=:memory:` answers a `CreatedLibraryDatabase` and creates no backups folder.

**Acceptance.** After the remedy lands, `LibraryDatabase.recreate` MUST keep the old file in the backups folder before it creates a new library; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recreate copies the old library file into the backups folder, then creates a new stamped library` and `recreate of an in-memory library creates a new one and copies nothing`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s11 invariants MUST pass.
